						<td class="body">
							Shadows Of Honor Charter      5 parts <br />
<br />
Where the value of every outlook....will not bring harm or censure back upon the guild.  <br />
<br />
Each of us who are enjoying Ever Quest and looking for &quot;the right fit&quot; in a guild has personal reasons for doing so, along with the practical reasons which are stated in the charter below. Those reasons vary from person to person, but we felt it may be helpful for others to know our visions, to understand the foundation of this guild, and perhaps to share with us part of what drives us to build it. Most of us, and certainly our officers, have been in other guilds in the past, guilds that have disappointed us. We are striving to make sure that those disappointing elements are not present in our new guild, Shadows of Honor. We will draw upon the experience of our high level alts for leadership to that end. <br />
<br />
Charter: <br />
Shadows of Honor was founded on the ideals of family and equality. Shadows of Honor are a group of adventurers bound together by the common calling to fight evil and to spread good, anonymously, as good deeds are meant to be done in order to give grace to the receiver, throughout Norrath. Above all else, Shadows of Honor values honor, fairness, compassion and harmonious fellowship. To be a member of Shadows of Honor is akin to being in a loving family, held together by the unbreakable bonds of friendship and loyalty. <br />
  <br />
It will be fun and intersting, not to mention rewarding, to develop ways of helping others anonymously. Examples: Healing or buffing someone from afar, or in a crowd; killing a mob then running away quickly; presenting a gift and saying something like &quot;that druid who just passed by here asked me to give you this&quot;, then gate or run away, as if in a hurry. <br />
<br />
Try to put SOME roleplay into this, develop your own EQ <br />
Shadows &quot;personality&quot;, (as part of the vision).						</td>
